From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: add SM6375 NoC provider driver

Six providers (bimc, clk_virt, config_noc, mmrt_virt, mmnrt_virt, sys_noc),
94 nodes, translated from the vendor holi.c (holi is SM6375) against
mainline's qcm2290.c, which is the same SMD-RPM architecture.

Note the ID split, which is not cosmetic. of_icc_xlate_onecell() uses the ID
written in the device tree *as an index into that provider's node array*, so
the binding has to number its nodes densely from 0 within each bus. But
icc_node_create() registers every node in one global IDR, so the .id field has
to be unique across all six. mainline qcm2290 solves this with two sets of
names and so does this driver: bare names in the binding for the array index,
SM6375_* in an internal enum for .id and .links.

The vendor header numbers all 94 nodes in a single global sequence, which was
carried over verbatim in the first version of this patch. That produced arrays
indexed 0..576 with only 9 to 44 real entries - bimc_nodes alone had 505 NULL
holes - and qnoc_probe() dereferences the first hole it reaches:

	Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at 0x0000000000000068
	pc : qnoc_probe+0x2dc/0x47c
	Call trace: qnoc_probe -> platform_probe -> really_probe

The compatible strings follow mainline's short forms, "qcom,sm6375-snoc" and
"qcom,sm6375-cnoc", the way qcm2290.c spells them, rather than "-sys-noc" and
"-config-noc". The device tree nodes were written with the short forms and the
match table with the long ones, so on the first boot with a matching DT only
bimc bound and the other five providers were silently never probed.

Add an SMD-RPM interconnect provider for the Qualcomm SM6375 (Snapdragon
695), needed so the IPA (mobile data) can vote its NoC bandwidth paths.
Without it, enabling IPA resets the SoC because the GSI hardware is
configured with the memory/config buses unvoted.

The driver mirrors the mainline sm6115.c driver (same SMD-RPM NoC family)
and is derived from the downstream Motorola SM6375 (holi) interconnect
tables. It describes the six buses (bimc, sys_noc, config_noc and the
clk_virt/mmrt_virt/mmnrt_virt virtual buses) with 104 nodes. QoS ports and
priorities for shared nodes match the mainline qcm2290/sm6115 drivers
(verified: qxm_ipa = qos_port 3, FIXED, prio 2). The RPM bus clock
descriptors and per-bus regmap register windows also match sm6115.

The binding header qcom,sm6375.h is copied from the downstream
qcom,holi.h (holi == SM6375); the ICBID values are the mainline RPM ids.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm6375.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1789 @@
